course: dictionary
lesson: 10522
title: Typhoid and the words around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Science texts often use hard names for illnesses. The words around them tell you what they mean. «Travellers to some countries need extra vaccines or medicines, such as against typhoid or yellow fever, and a travel nurse advises which ones.» Vaccines and medicines are used to protect people, so typhoid is an illness you can be protected from.
explain: Typhoid is caused by bacteria and caught from dirty water or food. So it is an illness you can catch, not something you wear or eat on purpose. When you meet a new name, ask: what does the sentence say this thing does, or what can happen to people with it?
explain: A phrase like «typhoid fever» puts two words together. Fever tells you the body gets very hot and ill. The word «typhoid» names which illness it is. Clean water, washing hands and vaccines help stop it from spreading.
fact: «Typhoid» is a serious illness caused by bacteria.
fact: You can catch typhoid from dirty water or food.
fact: Typhoid gives a high fever, stomach pain and weakness.
fact: Typhoid is treated with antibiotics and can be prevented with a vaccine.
fact: «Typhoid fever» is the full name for this illness.
exercise: «Travellers to some countries need extra vaccines or medicines, such as against typhoid or yellow fever.» What is typhoid? | *A serious illness caused by bacteria | A sort of warm jacket | A kind of hot drink | A type of boat used on rivers
exercise: What can cause typhoid? | Cold weather in winter | Sunshine on a warm day | *Bacteria in dirty water or food | Eating too many sweets
exercise: Which symptoms does typhoid give? | Cold feet and itchy ears | Bright red hair | *High fever, stomach pain and weakness | Loud laughing and jumping
test: What helps protect people from typhoid? | Staying in bed all day | *A vaccine | Wearing a hat | Eating more sweets
test: In the past, why did typhoid kill many people in crowded cities? | Everyone there had too much sunshine | People ate too many vegetables | Cities were too quiet | *Dirty water and poor sewers spread it
exam: Which of these best stops typhoid from spreading? | Eating only fruit | Sleeping with the windows shut | *Drinking clean water and washing hands | Playing outside in the rain
